## V1 to V2 material-survival audit

| Material or move | Decision | Target-linked reason |
|---|---|---|
| Hedione HC | REMOVE/REBASE | Local identity resolution collapses it with Hedione; its volume was consolidated into one regular-Hedione void rather than counted as false complexity |
| Tonka Bean Absolute 10% | REMOVE/REBASE | Modeled OAV 0.28 did not audibly own natural seed complexity; Coumarin and Tonkarome retain the protected warm nucleus |
| Dihydro Beta Ionone | REMOVE/REBASE | Modeled OAV 0.32 duplicated the stronger Alpha Ionone/AIMI/Irotyl complexion path |
| Cedramber | REMOVE/REBASE | Modeled OAV 0.47 duplicated cedar edge already carried by literal Cedarwood, Timberol, and Iso E space |
| Clearwood | REMOVE/REBASE | Modeled OAV 0.04 could not own fermented depth at practical allocation |
| Vertofix | REMOVE/REBASE | Modeled OAV 0.32 duplicated the more audible Vetikon cedar/vetiver bridge |
| Amberwood F | REMOVE/REBASE | Modeled OAV 0.20 added a generic amberwood label without distinct pressure; Ambrofix, Timberol, Kephalis, and diluted Norlimbanol retain separated contour roles |
| Beta-Pinene | REDOSE/REDILUTE | Rebased from 30 uL neat, modeled OAV 33810, to 10 uL of 10% stock, modeled OAV 1138, so it frames Cardamom EO rather than replacing it |
| Javanol | REDOSE/REDILUTE | Rebased from 100 uL neat, modeled OAV 16179, to 30 uL of 10% stock, modeled OAV 490, preserving mineral sandalwood contour without a Javanol-dominant perfume |
| Orivone | REDOSE/REDILUTE | Rebased from 80 to 10 uL neat, modeled OAV 858, preserving the iris-to-wood stitch without an Orivone-led heart |
| Ethyl Linalool, Irotyl, Himalayan Cedarwood, Kephalis | REDOSE/REDILUTE | Each was moved just above modeled OAV 1 so its named transition/character function is testable rather than decorative |
| Suederal | KEEP_STRUCTURAL | OAV 0.138; kept below leather recognition as one explicit pressure-texture exception; remove later if the seam ablation shows no benefit |
| Benzyl Salicylate, Hexyl Salicylate, Benzyl Benzoate | KEEP_STRUCTURAL | Three deliberately quiet matrix rows own bloom, green-floral continuity, and solvent/fixative mass; they are not counted as audible complexity |
| Bontoux Cinnamon Oil | HOLD | Missing plant-part identity and core physics prohibit strict OAV interpretation; the user-observed 10% preference supports only this controlled stock presentation |

No module moved more than 15% from its approved starting raw-volume budget. The cold shell is 660 uL (+10%), lavender prism 700 uL (-6.7%), iris/suede seam 290 uL (-3.3%), and every other module remains at its starting total.

## Governed anti-drift decisions

- Cardamom EO, Bontoux lavender, the Coumarin/Tonkarome floor, available cedar/vetiver, and Ethylene Brassylate form the protected LNDL nucleus.
- Bontoux cinnamon is a dry bridge, not a named cinnamon note. A pastry, candy, or Apple Pie reading fails the target.
- Ionones, Irotyl, and Suederal are surface tailoring. Lipstick iris, makeup, or leather dominance fails the target.
- The sandalwood and pressure rows are differentiated candidates, not a license for a woody-amber wall. Any modeled or physical takeover requires compression.
- No Tonalide, Macrolide, Musk Ketone, Habanolide, or Romandolide is present.
- Lemonile, Verdox, Verdyl Acetate, all tinctures, depleted Lemon FCF, depleted Cedarwood Virginia, and unavailable Gamma Decalactone are excluded.

## Preparation ledger

`DIRECT` means dose the owned, correctly labeled stock at the listed aliquot. `PREPARE_10_PERCENT` means the desired neat equivalent is below the 10 uL raw-stock floor and must be delivered through the specified 10% w/w stock. `HOLD_LABEL` means the physical bottle exists but must not enter a skin-bound or release-bound batch until its identity and stock basis are documented.

